      {
        "id": 163724,
        "name": "Ironic",
        "username": "Ironic",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-05T22:43:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah I'm pretty curious how that one plays out. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Probably fine.</p>\n<p>The Sentinels is already possibly the best damage-dealer in the game, with decent tanking/healing.&nbsp; And we can be pretty certain that Medico and Mainstay as solo heroes will just pile on more healing and tanking (respectively), whilst virtually every hero brings some damage with them.&nbsp; So the only real question is, is either Writhe or the Idealist good at Ongoing/Environment destruction?&nbsp; If so, you're set.&nbsp; If not, you get the same issues as any team which lacks that capability.</p>",
